('127.889.d.15.I',3,'An engine shows low oil pressure during a run, so the mechanic checks the oil level, pressure gauge and relief valve. She is:','["ignoring the gauge", "painting the gauge", "troubleshooting an engine oil pressure malfunction", "guessing"]'::jsonb,2,'Low oil pressure.','original'),
('127.889.d.15.I',4,'A common cause of low oil pressure is:','["a full tank", "cold fuel", "clean oil", "low oil level or a stuck-open relief valve"]'::jsonb,3,'Pressure cause.','original'),
('127.889.d.15.J',3,'The oil temperature gauge reads high, so the mechanic checks the cooler, the thermostat and the oil level. She is:','["troubleshooting an engine oil temperature system", "guessing", "ignoring the gauge", "painting the gauge"]'::jsonb,0,'High oil temp.','original'),
('127.889.d.15.J',4,'A blocked oil cooler would likely cause:','["clean oil", "high oil temperature", "low oil temperature", "low oil level"]'::jsonb,1,'Blocked cooler.','original'),
('127.889.d.15.K',3,'A mechanic uses a magnet and a lab chart to sort bits found in an oil filter into steel, aluminum and bronze. She is:','["ignoring metal", "painting metal", "identifying types of metal found in an oil filter", "buying metal"]'::jsonb,2,'Metal types.','original'),
('127.889.d.15.K',4,'Steel particles in an oil filter that stick to a magnet may come from:','["the seats", "the tires", "the window", "gears, bearings or cylinder walls"]'::jsonb,3,'Steel particles.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.A',3,'A student labels the magnetos, spark plugs, distributor and shower of sparks system on an engine ignition diagram. She is:','["identifying the components of ignition systems", "labeling seats", "labeling lights", "labeling tires"]'::jsonb,0,'Ignition parts.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.A',4,'The component that produces the high voltage for spark plugs in a magneto system is the:','["starter", "magneto''s coil", "oil pump", "alternator"]'::jsonb,1,'Mag coil.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.B',3,'A student explains how a magneto makes a spark with no battery as the engine turns. She is:','["avoiding theory", "describing seats", "explaining the operational theory of ignition systems and components", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,2,'Mag theory.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.B',4,'A magneto''s spark timing is set to fire:','["only at idle", "at random", "after the piston reaches top", "before the piston reaches top dead center"]'::jsonb,3,'Timing.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.C',3,'A student traces the starter motor, solenoid and gear that spin an engine to start it. She is:','["identifying the components and explaining the basic operation of engine starters", "describing seats", "avoiding starters", "describing tires"]'::jsonb,0,'Starters.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.C',4,'A starter solenoid acts as a:','["light", "heavy-duty switch that connects battery power to the starter", "tire valve", "fuel pump"]'::jsonb,1,'Solenoid.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.D',3,'A student studies how an igniter plug in a turbine combustor makes a spark to light the fuel. She is:','["describing tires", "describing seats", "identifying the components and explaining the basic operation of turbine engine ignition systems", "avoiding igniters"]'::jsonb,2,'Turbine ignition.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.D',4,'A turbine engine ignition system is used mainly:','["never", "only on the ground", "all the time", "during start and sometimes for relight"]'::jsonb,3,'Ignition use.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.E',3,'A student reads that spark timing that is too early or too late can hurt a piston engine. She is researching:','["the risks of advanced and retarded ignition timing on piston engines", "no risks", "paint choices", "tire brands"]'::jsonb,0,'Timing risks.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.E',4,'Overly advanced ignition timing can cause:','["better power", "detonation and engine damage", "smoother running", "a cooler engine"]'::jsonb,1,'Advanced timing.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.F',3,'A student learns that a capacitor discharge system stores a lot of energy and can deliver a painful shock. She is researching:','["paint choices", "tire brands", "the risks of maintenance on engines with capacitor discharge ignition systems", "no risks"]'::jsonb,2,'CD ignition.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.F',4,'Before handling a capacitor discharge ignition unit, technicians must:','["start the engine", "touch the leads", "ignore it", "wait for the stored energy to dissipate and follow the manual"]'::jsonb,3,'Wait for discharge.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.G',3,'A student reads that a magneto-equipped engine can fire if the propeller moves, even when the switch is off but the P-lead is loose. She is researching:','["the risks of working around reciprocating engines with an ignition system that is not grounded", "tire brands", "no risks", "paint choices"]'::jsonb,0,'Hot mag.','original'),
('127.889.d.16.G',4,'A grounded P-lead is what keeps a magneto:','["from starting", "from producing a spark when the switch is off", "from charging", "from cooling"]'::jsonb,1,'P-lead.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
